  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently focused on an active investigation regarding the alleged wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto. As law enforcement authorities continue their probe, the National Police have requested protection from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) for six individuals identified as witnesses. The investigation has drawn commentary from various sectors, including political parties like Gerindra and Golkar, as well as constitutional law experts who suggest the severity of the allegations could involve elements of treason. Furthermore, senior religious figures have publicly called for a comprehensive resolution to the case. Amid these developments, the President engaged in consultations with ten former National Police chiefs at his estate in Hambalang, a move reported by multiple national media outlets as the administration manages the implications of the security breach.",
